# Hub iframe = lobby roots only

**Incident:** Hub `iframeSrc` used `/play`, `/campaign`, `/rush/blitz`. On SPA hosts those paths are not static files → SPA fallthrough served the **parent website** inside the iframe.

## Hard rule

| Surface | Allowed `src` / `iframePath` |
|---------|--------------------------------|
| Hub `GamesSection` `iframeSrc` | `/games/<slug>/` only (or static `/games/<slug>/index.html`) |
| Embed registry `iframePath` | Same lobby root — never deep client routes |

```text
✅ /games/<slug>/
❌ /games/<slug>/play
❌ /games/<slug>/campaign
❌ /games/<slug>/rush/blitz
```

**First emotion** = lobby CTAs *inside* the game after lobby loads — not hub iframe deep-links.

## Contracts that must stay green

- Fleet Hub Tests: `tests/games/fleet-hub-fixes.test.mjs` — lobby-root only
- Host Metadata Tests: `tests/hub-iframe-titles.test.mjs` — forbids `/play|/rush/|/campaign` in hub iframeSrc

## Playtest / ship gate

Before claiming games hub OK: open `#games/<slug>`, assert iframe `src` is lobby root **and** iframe document is the game shell (brand in title/body), not parent site chrome.

## Do not

- “Fix first emotion” by pointing hub iframe at `/play` or `/campaign`
- Let host hub tests assert deep links while registry asserts lobby roots
- Playtest only `/games/<slug>/` and skip hub `#games/<slug>` iframe checks
- Treat display-name direct URLs as hub `iframeSrc` when they are aliases rather than canonical lobby roots.

Details → `create-web-game.mdc` §12.
